@lang en
-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
-- The rules of reading in Part 4 that ie-operation-and-construction.l4 does not hold: the lead-in of section 18; paragraphs (a) singular and plural,
-- (c) person, (j) offences by corporations and (i) time by reference to an hour; section 19 (a word in a statutory instrument); section 20(2) (other
-- parts of speech and grammatical forms of a defined word).
-- Each is a function over a small typed representation of what the rule operates on, tested on both sides of each limb.
-- Paragraphs (b), (d), (e), (f), (g) and (h) of section 18 are in ie-operation-and-construction.l4 and ie-interpretation-time.l4, and are not repeated.
--
-- PRECONDITION, STATED ONCE (section 4(1)): as in the other modules, the functions assume that no contrary intention appears in the enactment.
-- Section 19 takes that fact as an input because the section applies "in the statutory instrument" and names the enabling enactment, and the
-- lead-in of section 18 is exactly the application of section 4(1) to the paragraphs that follow it.
--
-- BORROWED FACT. Section 18(i) sends a time expressed by reference to an hour to the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971, which is not in the text
-- of this Act. The function for it asks the borrowed fact as an input: the offset from UTC of the standard time that Act fixes for the day.
-- `the clock time of a specified hour in an enactment` in ie-interpretation-time.l4 stays as the answer when no offset is supplied: it refuses.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`

§ `Named refusals`

-- One definition per refusal; each name is its message.

-- src:168 | (c) Person. “Person” shall be read as importing a body corporate (whether a corporation aggregate or a corporation sole) and an unincorporated body of persons, as well as an individual, and the subsequent use of any pronoun in place of a further use of “person” shall be read accordingly;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(c) (src:168)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 18(c) names the kinds of party that person imports, so a party of another kind is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 18(c) names the kinds of party that person imports, so a party of another kind is not answered"

-- src:179 | (j) Offences by corporations. A reference to a person in relation to an offence (whether punishable on indictment or on summary conviction) shall be read as including a reference to a body corporate.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(j) (src:179)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 18(j) names offences punishable on indictment or on summary conviction, and says nothing of an offence punishable in another way` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 18(j) names offences punishable on indictment or on summary conviction, and says nothing of an offence punishable in another way"

-- src:180 | Construction of statutory instruments. 19.—A word or expression used in a statutory instrument has the same meaning in the statutory instrument as it has in the enactment under which the instrument is made.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 19 (src:180)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 19 yields to a contrary intention under section 4(1), and the Act does not say what the word means then` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 19 yields to a contrary intention under section 4(1), and the Act does not say what the word means then"

-- src:178 | (i) Time. Where time is expressed by reference to a specified hour or to a time before or after a specified hour, that time shall be determined by reference to the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 ;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(i) (src:178)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 18(i) speaks of a specified hour, so an hour that is not a whole number from 0 to 23 is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 18(i) speaks of a specified hour, so an hour that is not a whole number from 0 to 23 is not answered"

§ `Section 18, lead-in: the rules apply to the construction of an enactment`

-- src:163 | General rules of construction. 18.—The following provisions apply to the construction of an enactment:
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18, lead-in (src:163); applies s 4(1)
GIVEN where IS A `Where a contrary intention appears`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section 18 rules apply to the construction of the enactment` where MEANS
    `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` where

§ `Section 18(a): singular and plural`

DECLARE `A grammatical number` IS ONE OF
    singular
    plural

-- src:164 | (a) Singular and plural. A word importing the singular shall be read as also importing the plural, and a word importing the plural shall be read as also importing the singular;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(a) (src:164)
GIVEN imports IS A MAYBE `A grammatical number`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A grammatical number`
`the numbers a word is read as importing` imports MEANS
    CONSIDER imports
    WHEN NOTHING          THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST singular    THEN LIST singular, plural
    WHEN JUST plural      THEN LIST plural, singular

-- src:164 | (a) Singular and plural. A word importing the singular shall be read as also importing the plural, and a word importing the plural shall be read as also importing the singular;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(a) (src:164)
GIVEN imports IS A MAYBE `A grammatical number`
      asked IS A `A grammatical number`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a word importing` imports `is read as also importing` asked MEANS
    elem asked (`the numbers a word is read as importing` imports)

§ `Section 18(c): person`

DECLARE `A kind of party` IS ONE OF
    individual
    `a corporation aggregate`
    `a corporation sole`
    `an unincorporated body of persons`
    `a party of another kind`

-- src:168 | (c) Person. “Person” shall be read as importing a body corporate (whether a corporation aggregate or a corporation sole) and an unincorporated body of persons, as well as an individual, and the subsequent use of any pronoun in place of a further use of “person” shall be read accordingly;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(c) (src:168)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of party`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the word person is read as importing` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN individual                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation aggregate`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation sole`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an unincorporated body of persons`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a party of another kind`               THEN `section 18(c) names the kinds of party that person imports, so a party of another kind is not answered`

-- src:168 | (c) Person. “Person” shall be read as importing a body corporate (whether a corporation aggregate or a corporation sole) and an unincorporated body of persons, as well as an individual, and the subsequent use of any pronoun in place of a further use of “person” shall be read accordingly;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(c), the pronoun limb (src:168)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of party`
      `a pronoun is used in place of a further use of person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` k `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` `a pronoun is used in place of a further use of person` MEANS
    IF   `a pronoun is used in place of a further use of person`
    THEN `the word person is read as importing` k
    ELSE FALSE

§ `Section 18(j): offences by corporations`

DECLARE `How an offence is punishable` IS ONE OF
    `on indictment`
    `on summary conviction`
    `in another way`

-- src:179 | (j) Offences by corporations. A reference to a person in relation to an offence (whether punishable on indictment or on summary conviction) shall be read as including a reference to a body corporate.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(j) (src:179)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of party`
      h IS A `How an offence is punishable`
      `the reference is to a person in relation to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` k `, the offence being punishable` h `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` `the reference is to a person in relation to an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the reference is to a person in relation to an offence` THEN FALSE
           IF h EQUALS `in another way` THEN `section 18(j) names offences punishable on indictment or on summary conviction, and says nothing of an offence punishable in another way`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER k
               WHEN `a corporation aggregate`  THEN TRUE
               WHEN `a corporation sole`       THEN TRUE
               WHEN individual                 THEN FALSE
               WHEN `an unincorporated body of persons` THEN FALSE
               WHEN `a party of another kind`  THEN FALSE

§ `Section 18(i): a time expressed by reference to a specified hour`

DECLARE `A moment in UTC` HAS
    `its day`                IS A DATE
    `its minute of the day`  IS A NUMBER

-- `its minute of the day` counts from the start of the day: 0 is the midnight at the start of `its day`, 1439 is one minute before the end of it.

-- src:178 | (i) Time. Where time is expressed by reference to a specified hour or to a time before or after a specified hour, that time shall be determined by reference to the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 ;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(i) (src:178); the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 is asked as an input
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      hour IS A NUMBER
      `minutes after that hour, or minus the minutes before it` IS A NUMBER
      `the offset in minutes ahead of UTC of the standard time that the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 fixes for that day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A moment in UTC`
`the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` day hour `minutes after that hour, or minus the minutes before it` `the offset in minutes ahead of UTC of the standard time that the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 fixes for that day` MEANS
    IF   hour LESS THAN 0 OR hour GREATER THAN 23 OR NOT ((TRUNC hour 0) EQUALS hour)
    THEN `section 18(i) speaks of a specified hour, so an hour that is not a whole number from 0 to 23 is not answered`
    ELSE LET total MEANS ((hour TIMES 60) PLUS `minutes after that hour, or minus the minutes before it`) MINUS `the offset in minutes ahead of UTC of the standard time that the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 fixes for that day`
         IN  `A moment in UTC` WITH
                 `its day`               IS day PLUS ((total MINUS (total MODULO 1440)) DIVIDED BY 1440)
                 `its minute of the day` IS total MODULO 1440

§ `Section 19: a word in a statutory instrument`

-- src:180 | Construction of statutory instruments. 19.—A word or expression used in a statutory instrument has the same meaning in the statutory instrument as it has in the enactment under which the instrument is made.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 19 (src:180); subject to s 4(1)
GIVEN `the meaning of the word in the enactment under which the instrument is made` IS A MAYBE STRING
      where IS A `Where a contrary intention appears`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the meaning in the statutory instrument of a word` `the meaning of the word in the enactment under which the instrument is made` `, a contrary intention being` where MEANS
    IF   NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` where
    THEN `section 19 yields to a contrary intention under section 4(1), and the Act does not say what the word means then`
    ELSE `the meaning of the word in the enactment under which the instrument is made`

§ `Section 20(2): other parts of speech and grammatical forms`

DECLARE `How a form of a word relates to the word an enactment defines` IS ONE OF
    `another part of speech of the word`
    `another grammatical form of the word`
    `a different word`

-- src:184 | (2) Where an enactment defines or otherwise interprets a word or expression, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the word or expression have a corresponding meaning.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 20(2) (src:184)
GIVEN rel IS A `How a form of a word relates to the word an enactment defines`
      `the enactment defines or otherwise interprets the word` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 20(2) gives the form a corresponding meaning` rel `, the enactment defining or interpreting the word` `the enactment defines or otherwise interprets the word` MEANS
        `the enactment defines or otherwise interprets the word`
    AND (CONSIDER rel
         WHEN `another part of speech of the word`     THEN TRUE
         WHEN `another grammatical form of the word`   THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a different word`                       THEN FALSE)
